{"qid":"Q202311","names":["Aq Qoyunlu"],"title":"Aq Qoyunlu","endonym":{"native":"ⲙⲏⲥⲣⲁ","lang":"cop"},"capsule":"The Aq Qoyunlu (White Sheep) was a Sunni Turkoman tribal confederation that ruled eastern Anatolia, Azerbaijan, and much of Iran and Iraq in the 15th century. Under Uzun Hasan it defeated the Qara Qoyunlu and became a major power, clashing with the Ottomans and Timurids. It collapsed in the early 16th century and was supplanted by the rising Safavid dynasty.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. This polity has not yet received individual source review: treat extents as indicative atlas convention.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Aq Qoyunlu","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Qara Yuluk Uthman Beg","nativeName":"قره یولوق عثمان بیگ","roman":"Qara Yūlūq ʿUthmān Beg","start":1407,"end":1435,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Ali Beg","nativeName":"علی بیگ","roman":"ʿAlī Beg","start":1435,"end":1438,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Hamza Beg","nativeName":"حمزه بیگ","roman":"Ḥamza Beg","start":1438,"end":1444,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Jahangir","nativeName":"جهانگیر","roman":"Jahāngīr","start":1444,"end":1457,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Uzun Hasan","nativeName":"اوزون حسن","roman":"Uzun Ḥasan","start":1457,"end":1478,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Khalil","nativeName":"خلیل","roman":"Khalīl","start":1478,"end":1478,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid